&lt;h3&gt;About SingleStore&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SingleStore delivers a real-time, distributed SQL database that unifies transactional and analytical workloads. Our engineers build cloud-native software for some of the world’s most demanding data-intensive applications, working in a fast-moving environment where teams own their work end to end and partner closely across Product and customer-facing organizations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the Flow team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SingleStore Flow is an enterprise data migration and integration product that helps customers move data into SingleStore reliably and at scale. The team builds the systems that support schema transfer, bulk data loading, real-time Change Data Capture (CDC), large-table migrations, and a native experience in SingleStore Helios.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Flow spans Java-based engines, source and destination connectors, database internals, performance and memory management, Helios services and APIs, observability, test automation, Flow AI Agent and signed production release delivery. The product works across heterogeneous database environments, including MySQL, PostgreSQL, Oracle, SQL Server, MongoDB, SAP HANA, Snowflake, Salesforce, and SingleStore-as-a-source.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Position Overview&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Staff Engineer to provide technical leadership for Flow’s end-to-end data path from source systems and CDC through migration engines, APIs, Helios, and the customer experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on individual contributor role with broad technical influence. You will own major architectural decisions, lead strategically important and release-defining initiatives, solve complex reliability and data-consistency problems, and help the team build durable systems that customers can trust with their most important migrations. You will remain close to the code while raising the technical bar for design, testing, observability, operational excellence, and AI-assisted engineering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate is a systems-minded engineer who enjoys working across product boundaries, can move comfortably between architecture and implementation, and knows how to turn difficult customer problems into scalable product improvements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Set technical direction for significant areas of Flow, including the migration engines, CDC pipeline, schema evolution, large-table migration, source-to-target data correctness, Flow APIs, Helios integration, and agent-assisted migration workflows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lead the design and delivery of large, complex, release-defining projects from problem definition through production rollout.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Make pragmatic architecture and build-versus-defer decisions that balance customer value, reliability, performance, maintainability, and delivery speed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Design and implement production-quality software while remaining hands-on in the codebase.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Solve difficult, ambiguous problems involving data consistency, replication, schema drift, throughput, memory use, concurrency, failure recovery, and backward compatibility.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Establish a high bar for technical design, code quality, testing, observability, security, and operational readiness.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Drive root-cause analysis for customer-impacting issues and ensure that incidents result in durable fixes, better tests, improved diagnostics, or clearer operational safeguards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Improve the team’s ability to operate Flow in production through runbooks, dashboards, release discipline, incident response, and shared ownership of service health.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Partner closely with Product Management, Engineering, Support, Solutions, and customers to translate real-world migration requirements into robust technical solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mentor engineers, lead design and code reviews, distribute technical context, and help develop the next generation of technical leaders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Create clear technical documentation that makes architecture, APIs, customer journeys, trade-offs, and operational procedures understandable to the broader engineering organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Advance AI-native development practices and agentic capabilities that improve engineering productivity and make customer migrations more self-serve.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
