&lt;h1&gt;SVP, Americas Sales&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Remote, Americas&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reports to:&lt;/strong&gt; Chief Revenue Officer&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About SingleStore&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SingleStore helps leading enterprises break free from legacy systems and fragmented data architectures with a unified, cloud-native data platform built for real-time transactions and analytics at scale. Our platform helps customers modernize data infrastructure, accelerate AI initiatives, and drive meaningful business transformation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our customers operate in data-intensive industries where performance, scalability, and data reliability are mission-critical. We partner with them to solve complex business and technical challenges and turn data into measurable outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The Opportunity&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SingleStore is seeking an accomplished, strategic, and execution-oriented sales leader to serve as SVP, Americas Sales. This executive will own the Americas go-to-market motion across Enterprise, Commercial, and Strategic segments, with leaders and teams rolling up to this role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The SVP, Americas Sales will be accountable for growth across new logo acquisition, expansion, forecast performance, and long-term customer value. This leader will set the operating rhythm for the Americas sales organization, develop a high-performing leadership team, and partner closely with the CRO and cross-functional executives to scale a predictable, value-led revenue engine.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an opportunity to shape the next phase of SingleStore’s growth while helping customers modernize their data environments and build the foundation for real-time applications and AI-driven initiatives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the Americas sales strategy and revenue plan across Enterprise, Commercial, and Strategic segments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate company priorities into clear regional goals, coverage models, account strategies, resource plans, and execution priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, coach, and develop the Americas sales leadership team, creating clarity of ownership and consistent standards across segments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a culture of accountability, urgency, customer obsession, and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive new logo acquisition, strategic account growth, cross-sell, expansion, and durable customer relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish a disciplined operating cadence for pipeline creation, opportunity progression, deal inspection, forecasting, territory planning, and performance management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve forecast accuracy and create clear visibility into risks, opportunities, conversion rates, coverage, and performance against plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide the organization through complex, multi-stakeholder enterprise transactions and ensure strong executive engagement throughout the sales cycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Account Executives, Sales Engineering, Value Engineering, Customer Success, Professional Services, Marketing, Product, Finance, and Operations to improve the full customer and revenue lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strengthen value-based and consultative selling practices, ensuring teams connect SingleStore’s technology to measurable business outcomes and the cost of inaction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop executive relationships with customers, prospects, partners, and industry influencers across the Americas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support strategic opportunities directly, including executive sponsorship, account planning, negotiation, close strategy, and customer relationship development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Marketing and Sales Development to improve ICP focus, pipeline quality, campaign alignment, and conversion from demand to qualified opportunity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Revenue Operations and Finance on territory design, capacity planning, compensation effectiveness, reporting, and business planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify organizational gaps and build the talent, structure, processes, and enablement needed to scale the Americas business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent SingleStore externally with credibility and serve as a senior voice of the customer internally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What Success Looks Like&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A clear and executable Americas strategy aligned to company priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consistent performance across Enterprise, Commercial, and Strategic segments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Predictable pipeline generation, opportunity progression, and revenue outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improved forecast accuracy and operating discipline across the sales organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong, accountable leadership team with clear ownership and effective succession depth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Increased executive-level engagement with strategic customers and partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A repeatable, value-led sales motion that differentiates SingleStore in complex enterprise environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stronger collaboration across Sales, Sales Engineering, Value Engineering, Customer Success, Marketing, Product, Finance, and Operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sustainable growth in new logo acquisition, expansion, retention, and customer lifetime value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You Bring&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years of enterprise software, cloud, data infrastructure, SaaS, or related technology sales experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years in progressive sales leadership roles, including responsibility for multiple teams, segments, or geographies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven success leading and scaling enterprise sales organizations across new logo, expansion, and strategic account motions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing through sales leaders and building high-performing, distributed teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of delivering revenue growth in complex, multi-year, consultative sales environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of enterprise technology buyers and data-driven transformation, including areas such as databases, analytics, cloud infrastructure, AI, distributed systems, or data platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
